@@ -4,3 +4,23 @@ target_include_directories(lightphysics_vhuman_face PRIVATE
     ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/include)
 set_target_properties(lightphysics_vhuman_face PROPERTIES
     C_STANDARD 11 C_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
+
+# Standalone CPU C ABI: no graphics, USD parser, CUDA, HIP or Python runtime.
+add_library(lightphysics_vhuman_full SHARED full.c
+    ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lightphysics/lightphysics_deformable.c
+    ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lightphysics/lightphysics_active_tissue.c
+    ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lightphysics/lightphysics_surface_contact.c
+    ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lightphysics/lightphysics_kinematics.c)
+target_include_directories(lightphysics_vhuman_full PUBLIC ${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/include)
+target_compile_options(lightphysics_vhuman_full PRIVATE -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic)
+if(UNIX)
+    target_link_libraries(lightphysics_vhuman_full PRIVATE m)
+endif()
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux")
+    target_compile_options(lightphysics_vhuman_full PRIVATE -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections)
+    target_link_options(lightphysics_vhuman_full PRIVATE
+        "-Wl,--version-script=${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/full.exports"
+        -Wl,--gc-sections -Wl,--no-undefined)
+    set_property(TARGET lightphysics_vhuman_full APPEND PROPERTY LINK_DEPENDS
+        ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/full.exports)
+endif()
diff --git a/examples/lightphysics_vhuman_face/README.md b/examples/lightphysics_vhuman_face/README.md
index 7067fa3..39c1d58 100644
--- a/examples/lightphysics_vhuman_face/README.md
+++ b/examples/lightphysics_vhuman_face/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,69 @@ with small or folded triangles.
 
 The output is a standalone facial patch for offline evaluation. It does not
 replace the head's skinned animation or estimate physical tissue parameters.
+
+## Full CPU facial ABI
+
+`lightphysics_vhuman_full` builds a standalone Linux/ELF shared library for
+the complete vhuman pipeline. It includes the CPU deformable solver, regional
+material moduli, energy-based Neo-Hookean XPBD, distributed active fiber
+stress, muscle activation dynamics, swept BVH vertex/triangle and edge/edge
+contact, final surface-crossing checks, and a force-driven reduced-coordinate
+mandible. It links only C code and libm. The old `VHSOFT1` experiment is separate.
+
+The full example's C ABI version is `vhface_full_abi() == 1`. vhuman's
+`VHFULL1` anatomy receipt and array package supply the tissue tetrahedra,
+fiber fields, muscle paths, bone attachments and original-surface embeddings.
+The caller owns excitation dynamics, inverse-control trials and complete
+state snapshots. Nodal impulses do not reset deformable constraints. Material
+tables are copied static configuration; muscle activation state belongs to
+the caller and must be saved with the deformable snapshot.
+
+`lightphysics_deformable_set_attachment_frames` supplies optional static normal
+frames and tangential compliances. A nonzero normal uses the attachment's
+ordinary compliance along that normal and the supplied compliance in its
+tangent plane. Zero normals keep isotropic behavior. Normals are normalized,
+inputs are copied transactionally, and replacing attachments clears frames.
+Snapshot restore requires identical static frames. The caller transports
+frames when supporting bones rotate. Guarded solving scales the full vector
+correction and its world-space XPBD multiplier together. The legacy
+`read_attachment_impulses` function returns multipliers in kg m, so tissue
+forces use the attachment weight divided by squared substep length and anchor
+forces use the opposite sign. vhuman supplies unit attachment weights.
+
+The mandible has bounded opening, lateral slide and forward slide. Vertical
+motion follows an authored condylar track. Tissue attachment and surface-contact
+reactions enter its generalized forces; there is no trajectory motor. Muscle
+directions, strength, tissue parameters and hidden anatomy remain authored
+animation priors, not measured physiological parameters.
+
+`lightphysics_surface_contact_find_intersections` enumerates the same proper
+edge/triangle events as the final crossing counter. Each record contains two
+edge vertex indices and three triangle vertex indices. Output is bounded by
+the caller's record capacity while the returned count always reports the full
+number of events. The query does not mutate positions or physical state. This
+supports offline CPU source-geometry fitting without weakening the bake gate.
+
+Implicit active tissue enables guarded tetrahedral solving. Inertia, material,
+fiber, volume and explicit attachment corrections use continuous signed-volume
+line searches; local corrections check every incident tetrahedron and scale
+their XPBD multiplier with the accepted displacement. The determinant's
+interior extrema are checked, including paths whose endpoint becomes positive
+after an inversion. Vertex/tetrahedron incidence is immutable configuration,
+while query stamps are transient scratch state. The caller must still validate
+post-solve contact projections and restore rejected complete states. Guarded
+solving is optional through `lightphysics_deformable_enable_guarded_solve`;
+owner projectors can use `lightphysics_deformable_project_guarded` for balanced
+double-precision corrections. This does not turn authored strengths into
+measured physiological parameters.
+
+Small corrections can use conservative per-vertex reference balls. Their
+radii bound the full determinant change by multilinearity, including the
+whole straight path. Leaving a ball invalidates fast proofs at every vertex
+of all incident tetrahedra; affected corrections use the exact cubic search.
+Bounds are rebuilt each solver sweep. Owner projectors used with guarded
+solving must apply changes through the guarded API.
+When all tissue tetrahedra are free, the inertial guard preserves mass-weighted
+translation and limits only relative motion. This keeps its volume safeguard
+from damping net center-of-mass momentum. Pinned tetrahedra retain their fixed
+vertices instead.
